// expect-error: does not fit 'u21'
// A global uN initialized with a constant expression that does NOT fit the
// width is rejected. (Until 2026-09-05 this file rejected `1000 + 500` because
// literal arithmetic was u32-typed and u32 -> u21 was a narrowing; LIT-2 now
// types a pure-literal tree by its destination and folds it WIDTH-EXACTLY, so
// `u21 g = 1000 + 500;` is accepted — see tests/zer/global_uN_const_expr.zer —
// and only an over-width result is refused.)
//
// TRIPWIRE (unchanged in spirit): the global emit path does NOT mask uN
// initializers. That is sound ONLY because every accepted constant expression
// fits the width by construction (the width-exact fold rejects anything else).
// If this file ever COMPILES, that guarantee is gone and the global emit path
// must mask the result to the width. Do not delete this test without adding
// that mask.
u21 g = 2097151 + 1;
u32 main() { return 0; }
